## [:< ##

# name  = users.record.optional_fields
# descr = fields a record MAY carry but is not created with
# param = -none-

## the authority's vocabulary of OPTIONAL fields, alongside
## users.record.default_fields' mandatory ones.  a record is created with the
## defaults ; these are what a user-edit console offers to ADD, and what any
## other client sees as the same vocabulary rather than inventing its own
## ad-hoc key names.
##
## NAMES MUST MATCH ^\w+$ -- they become ascii.frame slot tokens, and
## user-edit.form.schema_from_record skips anything else, so 'full_name'
## rather than 'full-name'.  the value is the field's STARTING SHAPE, and the
## shape IS the declaration : [] makes a collapsible multi-value list exactly
## as contact is, '' makes a plain line.
##
## EXTEND HERE.  this list is deliberately small -- it is a starting
## vocabulary, not a closed model, and adding to it costs one line.

return {
    qw| full_name | => '',
    qw| phone |     => [],
    qw| shell |     => '',
    qw| timezone |  => '',
};

